25: </style><body><main><header><span class="word">Orbs</span><small>DESIGN SYSTEM / 1.0 · MOBILE + WEB</small><button id="theme" class="orb-button">Dark mode</button></header>
26: <h1>A little context.<br>A natural next step.</h1><p class="intro">An interface that stays close to your attention. Quiet monochrome surfaces, fine moving lines, and just enough UI to carry an intention into action.</p><div class="tag">HACKATHON HANDOFF · 10 OCTOBER 2026</div>
27: <section><div class="sec-head"><h2>01 / One Ring. Four behaviors</h2><small>Selected Ring direction</small></div><div class="grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr))">
28: <div class="spec"><div class="orb-stage"><span data-state="breathing" aria-hidden="true"></span></div><h3>Ready</h3><p class="muted">A ring that slowly morphs. Present and available, with no task underway.</p><code>state: breathing</code></div><div class="spec"><div class="orb-stage"><span data-state="listening" aria-hidden="true"></span></div><h3>Listening</h3><p class="muted">The same ring expands and contracts with an irregular speech-like rhythm.</p><code>state: breathing</code><p class="preview-note">Selected irregular pulse; not microphone-reactive.</p></div>
29: <div class="spec"><div class="orb-stage"><span data-state="thinking" aria-hidden="true"></span></div><h3>Thinking</h3><p class="muted">The same ring turns smoothly and continuously while interpreting context.</p><code>state: breathing</code></div>
30: <div class="spec"><div class="orb-stage"><span data-state="acting" aria-hidden="true"></span></div><h3>Acting</h3><p class="muted">The same ring advances in three deliberate bursts with short pauses.</p><code>state: breathing</code></div></div><p class="guidance">Selected Ring system: exact thinking-orbs breathing geometry across every state; wrapper motion distinguishes activity. Keep a visible text label; motion alone is never status.</p></section>
31: <section><div class="sec-head"><h2>02 / Black. White. Breathing room.</h2><small>No accent color required.</small></div><div class="swatches"><div><div class="swatch" style="background:#111111"></div>Ink<br><small>#111111</small></div><div><div class="swatch" style="background:#ffffff"></div>White<br><small>#FFFFFF</small></div><div><div class="swatch" style="background:#fafafa"></div>Canvas<br><small>#FAFAFA</small></div><div><div class="swatch" style="background:#f4f4f4"></div>Raised<br><small>#F4F4F4</small></div><div><div class="swatch" style="background:#666666"></div>Secondary<br><small>#666666</small></div><div><div class="swatch" style="background:#dedede"></div>Line<br><small>#DEDEDE</small></div></div><p class="guidance">Use gray for hierarchy, not decoration. Errors and success use icons and words. Dark mode reverses surface hierarchy without changing the identity.</p></section>
32: <section><div class="sec-head"><h2>03 / Familiar typography</h2><small>System sans. Native on each platform.</small></div><div class="types"><div><span style="font-size:48px;line-height:52px;letter-spacing:-.04em;font-weight:500">Orbs</span><small>Display · 48 / 52 · Medium<br>Mobile · 36 / 40</small></div><div><h2>From attention to action.</h2><small>Section · 28 / 34 · Medium</small></div><div><h3>You can make it.</h3><small>Card title · 18 / 24 · Semibold</small></div><div><span>Take the 17:32 train from Winterthur.</span><small>Body · 15 / 22 · Regular</small></div><div><span style="font-size:12px;color:var(--orb-muted)">CALENDAR · 18:05–21:30</span><small>Metadata · 12 / 16 · Medium</small></div></div></section>
33: <section><div class="sec-head"><h2>04 / Context stays in place</h2><small>Attention → question → result → confirmation</small></div><div class="two"><div><div class="demo"><div class="article"><div class="tag">ON YOUR SCREEN</div><h3>Agentic AI meetup · Zürich</h3><p class="muted">An evening of demos and conversation.<br>Today, 18:05–21:30.</p><div class="attention">“Am I free, and how do I get there from Winterthur?”</div></div><div id="desktop-card" class="orb-card"><span class="source">Event details</span><h3 id="result-title">One conflict, then you’re free.</h3><p id="result-body">Take the 17:32 train. You’ll arrive at 17:51.</p><div class="row"><span>Team sync</span><small>18:00–18:30 · overlaps</small></div><div class="row"><span>Winterthur → Zürich HB</span><small>19 min · direct</small></div><div class="row"><span>Move sync to 19:00?</span><small>Check before I act</small></div><div class="actions"><button class="orb-button" id="cancel">Cancel</button><button class="orb-button primary" id="confirm">Confirm</button></div><p class="preview-note">Illustrative data; no calendar or travel tools connected.</p></div></div><p class="guidance">Web / anchor 12px from the selected content. 360px card; 24px radius; 20px padding. Keep original page readable.</p></div><div><div class="phone"><div class="tag" style="text-align:center">9:41 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ORBS</div><div class="article" style="margin-top:32px"><h3>A moment worth exploring.</h3><p class="muted">You notice an event in an article. Your attention provides a candidate; your question gives it meaning.</p><div class="attention">Agentic AI meetup<br>Today · Zürich</div></div><div class="pill-row"><span class="orb-pill"><span id="live-orb" aria-hidden="true"></span><span id="live-label" role="status" aria-live="polite">Listening…</span></span></div><div class="orb-card"><span class="source">Event details</span><h3>You can make it.</h3><p>The next train gets you there before it starts.</p><div class="actions"><button class="orb-button primary">Add to calendar</button></div></div></div><p class="guidance">Mobile / compact bottom sheet, 16px side margins, above keyboard and safe area. An editable transcript and text alternative remain available.</p></div></div><div class="controls" style="margin-top:24px"><button class="orb-button" data-live="idle">Ready</button><button class="orb-button" data-live="listening">Listening</button><button class="orb-button" data-live="thinking">Thinking</button><button class="orb-button" data-live="acting">Acting</button><button class="orb-button" data-live="done">Done</button><button class="orb-button" data-live="error">Error</button></div><p class="preview-note">Manual state controls demonstrate appearance only. App state must follow real microphone/model/tool events.</p></section>
34: <section><div class="sec-head"><h2>05 / Motion with restraint</h2><small>Animate the transition, preserve the context.</small></div><table><tr><th>Use</th><th>Duration</th><th>Curve</th><th>Behavior</th></tr><tr><td>Card enters</td><td>320ms</td><td>.16, 1, .3, 1</td><td>8px upward · .98 → 1 · fade in</td></tr><tr><td>Card exits</td><td>160ms</td><td>.4, 0, 1, 1</td><td>4px downward · fade out</td></tr><tr><td>State change</td><td>200ms</td><td>.4, 0, .2, 1</td><td>Crossfade label / shape</td></tr><tr><td>Control feedback</td><td>120ms</td><td>.4, 0, .2, 1</td><td>Press scale .98</td></tr><tr><td>Reduced motion</td><td>Immediate</td><td>None</td><td>Static orb + truthful label</td></tr></table></section>
35: <section><div class="sec-head"><h2>06 / Build consistently</h2><small>Implementation contract</small></div><div class="grid"><div class="spec"><h3>Attention is context</h3><p class="muted">A soft grayscale patch can suggest the target. Voice or selection confirms it. Gaze alone never authorizes a write.</p></div><div class="spec"><h3>Actions stay explicit</h3><p class="muted">Show exactly what will change. Confirm before writes. Display Done only after success. Offer Undo only when it works.</p></div><div class="spec"><h3>Small, accessible UI</h3><p class="muted">44px targets, clear focus, editable transcript, polite status announcements, and static reduced-motion states.</p></div></div><p class="guidance">Use tokens.css, tokens.json, OrbsIndicator.tsx, orb-motion.css and README.md from the developer bundle. Reference sizes: 64px hero / 20px inline orb. Hero specimens use the exact 64px preset; the pill uses the exact 20px preset.</p></section><footer>ORBS / DESIGN KIT 1.0<br>Based on the supplied attention demo and orb / card screenshots. Motion and token values are proposed implementation decisions.<br>Reference: <a href="https://libraries.dev/orbs">Libraries.dev — Thinking orbs</a>. Exact thinking-orbs component bundled with React. MIT notices included in the developer bundle.</footer></main></body></html>
